    #Story 1
    scene image "11_the_fourth_night/04_story_1.png"
    "Story 1: Captain Craven"
    scene image "11_the_fourth_night/05_story_establishing.png"
    "A timid military captain lives in a nation where wars rage without pause."
    "His frequent retreats have caused his men to nickname him 'Captain Craven.'"
    "This morning, he walks around the base and orders his men to prepare for combat."

    scene image "11_the_fourth_night/06_argument.png"
    angrySoldier: "This idiot drank my beer last night!"
    drunkSoldier: "I SCHAID I was schorry! Whaddya want from me!"
    captain "Let's all calm down, okay? I'll go buy some more later."

    scene image "11_the_fourth_night/07_argument_1.png"
    lazySoldier "Sooo, I kinda forgot the details of today's operation?"
    seriousSoldier: "You're the one in charge of preparation!"
    captain "It's all right. I'll take care of getting everything ready."
    
    scene image "11_the_fourth_night/08_captains_troubles.png"
    "Daily, the captain finds himself mediating quarrels among his hot-blooded men."
    "And yet, he never treats them as anything other than his trusted fellows."
    
    scene image "11_the_fourth_night/09_dicipline.png"
    loudSoldier "Heeey, Captain Craven!"
    loudSoldier "Yeah, we're all sick of you. Any chance you can just go off and die somewhere?"
    "After finishing his rounds, the captain restores a temporary discipline."
    loudSoldier "All right. I'll head back and get ready for the operation."

    scene image "11_the_fourth_night/10_unaccounted_for.png"
    brawnySoldier: "Captain, that problem child from yesterday is unaccounted for."

    "Earlier, a young boy had volunteered for combat so he could avenge his parents."
    "But concerned for the boy's well-being, the captain had turned down his proposal."
    "Dark clouds gather as they ready for combat, matching the captain's mood..."
    
    scene image "11_the_fourth_night/11_fio_mr_monster.png"
    carrier "My substitute said these are stories of war related to last night's dreams."
    fio "Hmm, 'Stories of war,' huh?"
   
    scene image "blackscreen.jpg"
    "The girl always looked to be having fun as we traveled. She had been plagued by nightmares and spent untold nights in tears in her old life, 
    but she looked downright cheerful in the world of The Cage.
    Even though humans are at the whims of their emotions, it seems their souls shone brighter with each bout of emotional turmoil, and I could not understand why.
    But that was the first time that I knew I wanted to be human so I could see the world from the same perspective as her."
    
